## 🚀 Installation

### From Source

```bash
git clone https://github.com/umbc-sanjaylab/FSA_Bench.git
cd FSA_Bench
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Configure the Environment

```bash
conda create -n FSA_Bench python=3.10
conda activate FSA_Bench
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## 📊 Dataset

FSA-Bench comprehensively evaluates federated survival models on **10 real-world federated survival datasets** covering diverse clinical domains, patient populations, sample sizes, feature dimensionalities, event rates, censoring patterns, and federated client configurations.

To evaluate models under realistic federated healthcare environments, we preserve naturally occurring institutional or geographically defined partitions. This enables evaluation under heterogeneous and non-IID data distributions across multiple clients in realistic environments.

### Dataset Summary

| Dataset | Samples | Variables | Event (%) | Censoring (%) | # Clients | Data Link |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| **TCGA** | 6,084 | 283 | 30.50 | 69.50 | 7 | [Link](https://www.cancer.gov/ccg/research/genome-sequencing/tcga) |
| **Aids2** | 2,839 | 3 | 62.03 | 37.97 | 4 | [Link](https://rdrr.io/cran/MASS/man/Aids2.html) |
| **LeukSurv** | 1,043 | 4 | 84.28 | 15.72 | 24 | [Link](https://rdrr.io/cran/spBayesSurv/man/LeukSurv.html) |
| **Pbc3** | 349 | 12 | 17.48 | 82.52 | 6 | [Link](https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/pec/versions/2025.06.24/topics/Pbc3) |
| **Dialysis** | 6,805 | 2 | 23.56 | 76.44 | 67 | [Link](https://rdrr.io/cran/RcmdrPlugin.survival/man/Dialysis.html) |
| **Oropharyngeal Carcinoma** | 192 | 12 | 72.40 | 27.60 | 6 | [Link](https://rdrr.io/cran/invGauss/man/d.oropha.rec.html) |
| **cgd** | 128 | 8 | 34.38 | 65.62 | 4 | [Link](https://rdrr.io/cran/survival/man/cgd.html) |
| **uis** | 628 | 7 | 80.89 | 19.11 | 2 | [Link](https://github.com/graemeleehickey/hosmer-lemeshow/blob/master/edition2/uis.txt) |
| **scania** | 1,040 | 4 | 52.60 | 47.40 | 5 | [Link](https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/eha/refman/eha.html#scania) |
| **SEER** | 25,749 | 11 | 25.36 | 74.64 | 3 | [Link](https://seer.cancer.gov/) |

The datasets span a wide range of federation settings, from **2 clients (UIS)** to **67 clients (Dialysis)**, and include both small cohorts such as **cgd (128 samples)** and large-scale datasets such as **SEER (25,749 samples)**.

## 🤖 Survival Models

FSA-Bench evaluates the following survival models:

- **Fed. Kaplan-Meier (Fed. KM)**
- **Fed. AFT-Weibull**
- **Fed. CoxPH**
- **NNPH**
- **NNnPH**
- **LinearPH**
- **DeepPseudo**
- **DeepHit**
- **FedPDNN**
- **FedPLSTM**
- **FedPAttn**

## ⚙️ Experimental Protocol

- **5-fold cross-validation**
- **Centralized Learning (CL)** and **Federated Learning (FL)**
- Up to **50 federated communication rounds**
- **Early stopping** based on validation performance
- Consistent preprocessing and evaluation across datasets and models

## 📈 Evaluation

### Predictive Performance

- **Time-dependent C-index** — Measures model discrimination. Higher is better.
- **Integrated Brier Score (IBS)** — Measures survival probability prediction accuracy. Lower is better.
- **Negative Log-Likelihood (NLL)** — Measures probabilistic prediction accuracy. Lower is better.

### Statistical Analysis

Pairwise model comparisons are performed using statistical significance tests with multiple-comparison correction.

### Explanation Stability

Model explanations are evaluated using **SurvSHAP** across folds, federated sites, and centralized/federated partitions.

Stability is measured using:

- **Spearman's rank correlation**
- **Kendall's tau**
- **Jaccard similarity**

